g) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-178 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-179 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-144 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-146 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-147 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-148 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-149 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-150 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-151 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-152 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-154 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-155 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it is met at an interface, rests on an assumption or is a property of the whole system\r\nWARNING (advisory): SR SR-156 declares no Form (interface | assumption | cross-cutting) — say whether it","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"C:\\Users\\Peter\\AppData\\Roaming\\project-trajectory\\accounts\\ADJUDICATOR\\projects\\C--Projects-ai-template-wt-wi-956\\f031c6a5-ecf0-490f-9890-c7a8a87f92fc\\tool-results\\brfvx3y9s.txt","persistedOutputSize":83342,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-956\\docs\\reviews\\wi-956\\002-ADJUDICATE-a15f4b6.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":51,"lines":["+# WI-956 adjudication: plan critique 2, finding F1","+","+Range: `72c81fcdb3144109c8505cf7cb4c5e4f56ad7a80..39c6a4828c3a7771b9f65a4c002a9813523ac933`","+(plan, critiques 1 and 2). Ruled against PROCESS.md §6 \"Review threat model\",","+the WI-956 spec's Done-when, and `kitlib/verdict.py` at this range.","+","+## F1: `governing_rev` walks through an empty review carrier","+","+**What I observed.** I built a scratch repo: a work commit W, then a verified","+refresh R on top of it (the current grammar), then an empty","+`attest: lane bar=review` commit E carrying a `Bar-Green: ... bar=review","+tests=none` trailer whose tree and parent check out. At this range:","+`_peel_target(E)` is `None`, so the review commit is not peeled.","+`governing_rev` returns W and not E, and `governing_identity(tip)` equals","+`tree_identity(W)` and not `tree_identity(R)`. I swapped E for a plain empty","+telemetry commit and got the same result. So the finding describes the walk's","+behaviour correctly. An empty review carrier is walked through, and the refresh","+beneath it is peeled.","+","+**Why that is not a Done-when gap.** In this module, \"peel\" and \"walk\" are two","+different steps. `governing_rev`'s docstring defines the peel as \"the one step","+that does move the identity\", allowed only after `_peel_target` verifies the","+commit. A walk step is taken only when a commit's non-record identity equals its","+parent's, so a walk step can never change the answer. The Done-when says","+\"`work_tip` and `governing_rev` never peel a verified `review` attestation\".","+Deliverable 2 names how: `refresh_attestation` is narrowed to `bar` in","+{landing, no-bar}, and `_peel_target` keeps calling it. That is exactly what P2","+delivers. An empty review commit is not peeled. It is walked through, and that","+step cannot change the governing identity, because the commit carries no work.","+","+**Peeling the refresh beneath is correct.** It is the OI-76 fix this function","+exists for. A refresh is disposable, and an identity-neutral commit stacked on","+it must not hide it. Otherwise an APPROVE served before the refresh would stop","+governing, and the slot would refuse \"no logged review round names its current","+tree\".","+","+**The proposed fix would cause a regression.** Stopping the walk at a review","+carrier would shift the identity of tip E from W's tree to R's composed tree. A","+commit that changes nothing would then stale an honest pre-refresh verdict.","+","+**The finding's second scenario has no effect.** That scenario is \"returns the","+parent rather than the review commit\", with no refresh beneath. The only caller","+of `governing_rev` is `governing_identity`. It reads only the identity, and the","+walk's step condition makes the parent's identity equal the carrier's.","+","+Finally, a review attestation that carries a work change, the case where peeling","+would let unreviewed work through, is the case P2's","+`test_governing_rev_never_peels_a_review_attestation` already pins. The finding","+is accurate about the mechanics but wrong that they are a defect.","+","+RULING: F1 DISMISS refuted — an empty review carrier is walked through, not peeled. That step leaves the identity unchanged by construction, and `governing_identity`, the only consumer, reads only the identity. Peeling the refresh beneath is the intended OI-76 behaviour, and a stop at the carrier would stale an honest pre-refresh verdict."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-956\\docs\\reviews\\wi-956\\002-ADJUDICATE-a15f4b6.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019YWKFvjBuCfrar9GkBNXcG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
