{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDoZ6W2VqzUvDg8Vjjyu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled F1 **DISMISS refuted**. The verdict is committed as `f25567801`, with the commit hooks passing, in `docs/reviews/wi-956/002-ADJUDICATE-a15f4b6.md`.\n\n**What I checked.** I built a scratch repo: a work commit W, a verified refresh R on top of it, then an empty commit E carrying a valid `bar=review` attestation. On the code at this range:\n- `_peel_target(E)` returns `None`, so the review commit itself is not peeled.\n- `governing_rev` walks through E and peels R. It returns W, and the governing identity is W's tree.\n- A plain empty telemetry commit in E's place gives exactly the same result.\n\nSo the finding describes the mechanics correctly. It is wrong to call them a gap in the Done-when.\n\n**Why it's refuted:**\n- **\"Peel\" and \"walk\" are different steps in this module.** A peel is the one step that changes the identity, and it happens only after `_peel_target` verifies the commit. A walk step is taken only when a commit's identity equals its parent's, so it can never change the answer.\n- **The spec's mechanism is the one the plan delivers.** Deliverable 2 says how the Done-when is met: narrow `refresh_attestation` so `_peel_target` declines a review commit. P2 does exactly that.\n- **Peeling the refresh beneath is intended.** It is the OI-76 fix `governing_rev` exists for. The proposed stop at the review carrier would move the tip's identity from W's tree to the refresh's tree. A commit that changes nothing would then stale an honest verdict served before the refresh.\n- **\"Returns the parent, not the review commit\" has no visible effect.** `governing_rev`'s only caller is `governing_identity`, which reads just the identity, and the parent's identity equals the carrier's.\n- **The risky case is already tested.** That is a review commit that carries a work change, where peeling would let unreviewed work through. P2's `test_governing_rev_never_peels_a_review_attestation` covers it.\n\nI did not touch the `002-ADJUDICATE-a15f4b6.md.requested` marker. It was untracked before I started, so I left it for the coordinator."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":541,"cache_read_input_tokens":62182,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":541},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f031c6a5-ecf0-490f-9890-c7a8a87f92fc","uuid":"63d81515-9a04-4634-970a-26d32fd3fe69","timestamp":"2026-10-20T16:27:37.343Z","request_id":"req_011CgDoZ6BSNjUadtW1ZK3PE"}
